  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4a0043c5-fc59-5b65-8403-5057adca0f4f" activityNameId="d757e813-4bd3-576a-b404-40c816b0c6c0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Operation, aircraft, passenger, Europe</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Operation, aircraft, passenger, Europe
Average fuel consumption and emission data caused by an intra European flight. In order to transform tonne kilometre (tkm) performance in passenger kilomter performance (pkm) each passenger is accounted for with a mass of 240 kg. The place of departure is Switzerland. The emissions are given for three subcategories: low poulated are, startosphere and unspecified.;
UUID: 551527a2-f201-3f17-8e71-21292de41016
The invetory includes consumption of kerosene and direct emissions to air (gaseous emissions, particulate emissions, emissions of heavy metals)
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The data is calculated for today"s average aircraft technology
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: na
Sampling: national statistics, publications of environmental agencies, information from aviation companies 
Extrapolations: Swiss data is extrapolated to represent European conditions.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_551527a2-f201-3f17-8e71-21292de41016.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
